    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-13049",
      "problem": "The point shown below represents a number on a number line. The absolute value of this number is $4.$ What is the number?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14145654/assets/0e8aaf68af47ecf3eadbd492af662273a68400bed20d3a5b214ec118abb6a2df.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The number is *negative* because it is to the *left* of zero.\n\nThe absolute value of the number is $4,$ so the distance between that number and zero on a number line is $4.$ \n\nThe negative number at a distance of $4$ from zero is $-4,$ so the number is $-4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14145654/assets/b0d99997e27059b23342de79fc887c85b56991e1312f430f80fcf39311479ad2.png)",
